# Amazonbot crawls /join and /login ~200K times a day — 28% of every request ifttt.com
# serves — and Amazon states it feeds their products and AI model training rather than a
# search engine that refers traffic back to us. It honors per-agent disallow but not
# crawl-delay, so scoping it off the two auth pages is the only lever robots.txt gives us.
#
# Search and AI crawlers that DO refer traffic keep full access via User-agent: * above.
# /login ranks at position 1.8 for "ifttt login" and /join for "ifttt free"/"ifttt account";
# together they earn ~90 organic clicks a day. Do not move these two rules into the
# wildcard group — see web#10531, which removed a disallow near /join for the same reason.
#
# A crawler that matches a named group ignores User-agent: * entirely, so this group has
# to repeat every wildcard rule above. Adding a rule there means adding it here too.
